@startuml class-diagram-db-encryption
title Class Diagram (Implementation) — Local Database + Encryption
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam shadowing false
hide circle
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

class Database <<singleton module>> {
  +getDb() : DbHandle
  +initDatabase(filePath) : "Promise<DbHandle>"
  +recordStockMovement(db, params) : int
  +writeAuditLog(db, params)
  +mapProduct(row) : object
  +mapTransaction(row) : object
}

class DbHandle <<wrapper>> {
  +exec(sql)
  +prepare(sql) : Statement
  +transaction(fn) : function
}

class Encryption <<module>> {
  +getOrCreateKey(dbPath) : Buffer
  +encryptBuffer(plain, key) : Buffer
  +decryptBuffer(cipher, key) : Buffer
  +isEncrypted(buffer) : bool
}

Database ..> DbHandle : wraps raw sql.js Database in
Database ..> Encryption : encrypts on persist(), decrypts on load

note "persist() (private to db.js) is the only thing that ever writes the DB\nfile, and it always routes through Encryption.encryptBuffer — see\ndocs/compliance/data-protection.md." as N1
@enduml
